# `raw/NpcScript.cpp` is a byte-for-byte copy of the client's CRLF-only compile
# input, and the surgical writer + its tests assert that convention. Without
# this, Linux checkouts get LF (the index is normalized) and the writer emits
# LF, so the CRLF invariants fail on CI but pass on Windows.
packages/resources/raw/NpcScript.cpp text eol=crlf
